# ----------------------------------------------------------------------
# 1. Broad Ignore Rule (Example)
#    If you ignore all files/folders in the root, you must explicitly
#    un-ignore the ones you need.
# ----------------------------------------------------------------------

# Example: Ignore everything in the root, forcing explicit un-ignore below
# *

# Example: Ignore all compiled objects or binaries everywhere
# *.obj
# *.exe
# *.dll

# Example: Ignore all editor-generated local user files (e.g., VS, IDE)
# .vs/
# *.user
# *.vcxproj.filters
# *~

# ----------------------------------------------------------------------
# 2. Negation (Inclusion) Rules for Your Engine Structure
#    These lines ensure the specified folders and everything inside them
#    are NOT ignored, even if a broad rule above might apply.
# ----------------------------------------------------------------------

# Required Folders (Un-ignoring a folder ensures all its contents are tracked)

!/extern/
!/tools/
!/tools/**
!/engine/
!/engine/**
!/editor/
!/editor/**
!/shaders/
!/shaders/**
!/assets_raw/
!/assets_raw/**
!/assets_cooked/
!/assets_cooked/**
!/projects/
!/projects/**
!/cmake/

# Required Files (Un-ignoring the root CMakeLists.txt)
!/CMakeLists.txt

build/
hephaestus.log
**/hephaestus.log
logs/
**/.hephaestus/editor/